69
00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.770
Paul would have been a really interesting thing to banter about while we were on set

70
00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.690
waiting for lights to go up and stuff.

71
00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:40.790
He's holding back.

72
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.430
I did know he'd been to Russia.

73
00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:42.790
Oh.

74
00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.590
So there you go.

75
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:45.510
How was it?

76
00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.170
Was it great?

77
00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.090
It was great.

78
00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.790
He had a great, great time.

79
00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:57.290
Well, he said that he was so excited to be able to write and direct this episode because

80
00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:01.810
it featured the first visit to Dwight's farmhouse at Shroot FarMs.

81
00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:02.990
Because we've been there.

82
00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.670
We saw the barn in the initiation and all that.

83
00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:14.230
But he got to completely invent Dwight's home and what it looked like and all of that stuff.

84
00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:20.930
And he said that he got the idea for Dwight to run a bed and breakfast during a trip to Italy

85
00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.390
a couple of years before.

86
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.650
He is a world traveler.

87
00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:24.990
He's well-traveled.

88
00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:33.050
So while he was in Italy, he had seen a bunch of signs for this farm B&B stay.

89
00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:36.010
You go stay on people's farms in Italy.

90
00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.210
Sounds amazing.

91
00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:41.830
I just want Paul to know, if you're listening, Paul, you don't have to go all the way to Italy

92
00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:42.310
for that.

93
00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.490
You can have a farm B&B right here.

94
00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.630
I'm sure like my family farm in Texas would take you in.

95
00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.910
I would love to have a farm B&B experience at your parents' farm.

96
00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.010
I would love that so much.

97
00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.090
I would love to get up in the morning and go check on the cows with you.

98
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.210
Oh, lady, you're speaking my language.

99
00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:11.190
Well, Paul just said he loved imagining Dwight as a proprietor of a bed and breakfaSt.

100
00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.730
And he also told me he did so much to prepare for this episode.

101
00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:19.730
He really like overprepared because it was just a really big deal to him.

102
00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:22.590
And he wanted it to be full of so many details.

103
00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:23.870
And it was.

104
00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:24.810
Oh, yes.

105
00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.110
There's so many cool details.

106
00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.190
And we're going to point them out to you as they come up.

107
00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:29.290
Definitely.

108
00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:30.990
All right.

109
00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.810
Fast fact number two is a location breakdown.

110
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.570
I knew this was coming.

111
00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:38.110
The Shrute Farms location breakdown.

112
00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:40.810
I have been to this farm many times.

113
00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:41.690
Let's hear what you got.

114
00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:47.530
So we mentioned before that we shot Shrute Farms on the Disney Ranch in Santa Clarita,

115
00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.090
California.

116
00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.570
We went back for this episode.

117
00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:55.270
And this time we used the Olivia's House location.

118
00:04:55.270 --> 00:05:00.570
That is the farmhouse that we transformed into Dwight's B&B.

119
00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:05.490
Yes, you guys should know this is a vast property and they have different areas where they film.

120
00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.170
So they have the barn, right, where you saw the initiation.

121
00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:13.770
And then they have little houses and different areas that you can use to create sort of this

122
00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:15.670
rustic look for TV and film.

123
00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.890
But these houses, they're just shells.

124
00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.290
There's nothing in them.

125
00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:20.730
Nothing.

126
00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.290
They're just like exterior shell walls.

127
00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:25.030
The walls are not insulated.

128
00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:27.310
So it got very, very cold at night.

129
00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.290
Any of the night scenes, we were freezing.

130
00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:31.390
Freezing and drafty.

131
00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.090
And everything is a little bit dusty.

132
00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:37.430
Like if you sit on something, like a little cloud of like, yeah, it kind of comes out of it.

133
00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:44.110
And our set designers had to go in and they had to meticulously decorate every single room.

134
00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.370
Every item you see, we put there.

135
00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.130
That's right.

136
00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:47.690
That's right.

137
00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:51.150
I have a feeling they went in first and cleaned and then decorated.

138
00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:54.870
Why is my memory of shrewd parms so dusty?

139
00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.270
Well, I remember sneezing a lot.

140
00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.050
It's dusty.

141
00:05:58.610 --> 00:05:59.470
It's old.

142
00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:00.370
It's run down.

143
00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.850
You know, you wouldn't want to lean against the wall.

144
00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:04.050
I'll just say that.

145
00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:04.350
No.

146
00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.230
You might go right through it.

147
00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:09.350
Now, we have another location in this episode.

148
00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:12.150
Michael takes a job as a telemarketer.

149
00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:15.230
And I asked Kentopedia about this location.

150
00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:20.290
The exterior, when you see him walking into the building, we shot that in Van Nuys.

151
00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.410
That was near our studio.

152
00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:29.670
But the inside of the building, we shot on the 10th floor of the LA Times building in downtown LA.

153
00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.010
Now, this shocked me.

154
00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:36.850
This shocked me because this building is stunning.

155
00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.090
Stunning.

156
00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.070
It housed the LA Times until 2017.

157
00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:44.610
It was designed by this man named Gordon B.

158
00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.050
Kaufman in the Art Deco style in the 1930s.

159
00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:52.090
It won a gold medal at the 1937 Paris Exposition.

160
00:06:53.410 --> 00:07:05.590
And it's just, it's so weird to me that this very, like, ordinary telemarketing office is housed inside of this gorgeous piece of architecture.

161
00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:10.130
I know, that is so wild because we don't do that building justice at all.

162
00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:13.470
We make it look just like any cubicle office anywhere, right?

163
00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:13.850
Yeah.

164
00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:18.270
Well, I shot a commercial in my 20s in downtown LA.

165
00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:24.990
And I was really stunned because it was a gorgeous building and we were shooting on, like, the 12th floor.

166
00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:28.090
And then they had, like, craft and service on a different floor.

167
00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:29.550
You know, they used a few floors.

168
00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.630
And it was, like, three floors in a row with no people.

169
00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:33.490
No one.

170
00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:34.130
Wow.

171
00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:39.790
So, I think there are, like, sort of buildings downtown that have just a lot of vacancy.

172
00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.490
Yeah, there must be.

173
00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:42.170
I know.

174
00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:46.050
It was really eerie because we were filming at night and it was, like, a dark corridor.

175
00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:57.010
Well, I visited the LA Times back in college as part of a film and television summer workshop that was coordinated by UCLA.

176
00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:01.250
And we got to go in and see how they make newspapers.

177
00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.690
And I remember the lobby.

178
00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:06.490
It has this great big globe and I have all these pictures.

179
00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.350
It was just amazing.

180
00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.050
I would love that.

181
00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.070
I would sign up for that.

182
00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:11.670
Yeah.

183
00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.390
I mean, you know, I love a tour.

184
00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:15.870
We would sign up for almost any tour.

185
00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:16.790
I feel like.

186
00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:17.150
We would.

187
00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:24.190
I mean, I feel like we could do a podcast where it's just you and I taking tours and talking about today we went to the peanut factory.

188
00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.230
Oh, lady, that's a brilliant idea.

189
00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.030
We have to do that.

190
00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:32.990
We travel and go on tours and then tell people about the tour we went on.

191
00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.030
I mean, selfishly, I want to do that.

192
00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:35.910
That sounds great.

193
00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:37.050
Okay.

194
00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:38.150
Okay.

195
00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:44.570
Well, speaking of travel, fast fact number three, TripAdvisor features very heavily in this episode.

196
00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:45.310
Yes.

